# tests/check-box-layout.sh: what still goes around the layout owner
# (we_layout.c), per rule and file, with the pass that moves it.  The count
# may only fall; a line that matches nothing fails as stale.  Rules 1 and 4
# have no lines: they hold from the first pass.
#
# rule  file-or-object  count  pass
#
# Rule 2: e_close_view(pic, 0) drops a background by hand; the owner's stamp
# does it since P14a, so each goes with the box it belongs to.
drops we_ai_ui.c 2 P14c
drops we_menue.c 1 P14b2
drops we_opt.c 2 P14b1
drops we_wind.c 1 P14b1
# Rule 3: a box opens through wpe_box_open, which enters the screen owner
# itself.  The prefixes and readers with no box (we_mouse.c, we_term.c,
# we_prog.c) stay: P14c moves them onto the owner's no-box reader.
# The we_wind.c line is the error box (e_error_run, we_wind.c:616), P14b1.
modal we_ai_ui.c 4 P14c
modal we_menue.c 2 P14b2
modal we_mouse.c 1 P14c
modal we_opt.c 1 P14b1
modal we_prog.c 2 P14c
modal we_term.c 2 P14c
modal we_wind.c 1 P14b1
# Rule 5: an object that imports e_std_kst draws a frame by hand; a box's
# frame goes through wpe_box_frame.
stdkst we_ai_ui.o 1 P14c
stdkst we_debug.o 1 P14c
stdkst we_opt.o 1 P14b1
# Rule 5: e_open_view( calls per file.  The windows' own views (we_wind.c),
# the desk's keep-view and the mouse drags are not boxes and stay; the
# full-screen views of a command (we_prog.c, we_fl_unix.c) open through the
# owner's FULL_SCREEN rule in P14b2.
openview we_fl_unix.c 2 P14b2
openview we_menue.c 2 P14b2
openview we_mouse.c 3 keep
openview we_opt.c 1 keep
openview we_prog.c 1 P14b2
openview we_wind.c 5 keep
openview we_xterm.c 1 keep
